{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/405295-navigation-in-hedge","id":405295,"title":"Navigation in Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-13T17:02:12-08:00","id":405295,"title":"Navigation in Hedge","content":"Mine PCs ended last game divided and hurt in Hedge, running away from Charlatan and his hobgoblin guards. Now, the need to find way home, to mortal realm. I read the 1ed corebook rules and do not get them on walks in the Hedge, as they are bit contradictory. Nominally, those:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: The Lost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A changeling can search for an active gateway, and will probably find one, given enough time. This requires an extended action. The roll is Intelligence + Investigation + Wyrd. The time that each roll represents varies based on how familiar the character is with the surrounding area.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: The Lost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Long Walk: If you\u2019d rather just determine how long the walk takes and pick up the chronicle when the characters arrive at their destination, that\u2019s fine, too. Have each player roll Intelligence + Survival at the beginning of the journey. One character may guide the others, making this a cooperative roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: The Lost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">( About Trods )Finally, it\u2019s not impossible to get lost while keeping to a pathway. Every time a changeling in the Hedge chooses a goal or destination, his player must roll Clarity. Trying to navigate while not on a path incurs a \u20133 dice modifier on this roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for characters walking half blindly in Hedge - what rules should I use? Also - why would changeling step off in to the Thorns, if the pathways are psychoactive and he can just &quot;envision&quot; his destination, so the Hedge will make him a way to it?<br /> <br /> Bonus question: <b>I use modified Integrity stat in place of Clarity - called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/297978-changling-2-0-fan-idea-clarity-breaking-points?p=301896#post301896\">Dichotomy</a>.</b> Idea is that this is more fluid and changing statistic, even changing it value few times a game session. With this, I need to replace the Clarity roll on the Trods. Any idea what to use? Maybe <i>Wits+Wyrd</i> of character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-14-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T16:32:57-08:00","id":406189,"title":"","content":"The section of the book on the hedge is a little vague but my understanding is it works like this:<br /> <br /> To get to a specific location you roll Intelligence + Survival. This lets you navigate to an area of the hedge such as your hollow or the hedge reflection of your home city. You do need to be familiar with the place you're navigating to so you can't just arbitrary find your way anywhere altho with all the information available you can probably navigate to any moderately notable city and certainly any country on earth.<br /> <br /> Once you get to your destination you still need to find a way out of the hedge. That's where the Intelligence + Investigation comes in. You need to find an existing hedge gate (if one exists at all) before you can open it back to earth.<br /> <br /> So, lets say you're walking from SF to NY. First you enter the hedge. Then you navigate to the big apple with Intelligence + Survival. Finally you look for a gate out into the mortal city with Intelligence + Investigation.<br /> <br /> As for why changelings would go off the path? Generally they don't if they can avoid it. Sometimes they might dramatically fail a navigation test and accidentally stumble off. If a changeling is threatened on the path, say by a True Fae, it's easier to hide amongst the thorns than on a narrow trod. Some fruits might only grow deep in the brambles as well. In my game I made Hera Pears only grow off the path to add a little danger to their harvest.<br /> <br /> Finally, whatever you've moved Clarities bonus/penalties to perception and kenning onto should be what you base the Clarity rules in the hedge on. If it's tagged onto your new Integrity mechanic then just use that, even if it does change regularly. If you've gotten rid of those mechanics entirely... Well I'm not sure what you'd want to do about that at this moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T21:22:03-08:00","id":406334,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the post, <b>Helel</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/405295-navigation-in-hedge?p=406189#post406189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To get to a specific location you roll Intelligence + Survival. This lets you navigate to an area of the hedge such as your hollow or the hedge reflection of your home city. You do need to be familiar with the place you're navigating to so you can't just arbitrary find your way anywhere altho with all the information available you can probably navigate to any moderately notable city and certainly any country on earth.<br /> <br /> Once you get to your destination you still need to find a way out of the hedge. That's where the Intelligence + Investigation comes in. You need to find an existing hedge gate (if one exists at all) before you can open it back to earth.<br /> <br /> So, lets say you're walking from SF to NY. First you enter the hedge. Then you navigate to the big apple with Intelligence + Survival. Finally you look for a gate out into the mortal city with Intelligence + Investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, it's clearing things up to me. If I change a Freehold area, I use the Intelligence + Survival. When I found correct &quot;region&quot; - I use the Intelligence + Investigation + Wyrd to find a gateway. In mine example - as character do not leave the region ( their hometown Hedge ) and only looks for the nearest way out, just use &quot;Gataway roll&quot;?<br /> <br /> What about situation when they are actively hunting for the Goblin Fruits ( the are almost dead, they need their healing )? I assume looking for those is with the Intelligence+Survival? But if finding the clues for specific Gates is based on Investigation, maybe looking for the clues of Goblin Fruits should also?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/405295-navigation-in-hedge?p=406189#post406189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why changelings would go off the path? Generally they don't if they can avoid it. Sometimes they might dramatically fail a navigation test and accidentally stumble off. If a changeling is threatened on the path, say by a True Fae, it's easier to hide amongst the thorns than on a narrow trod. Some fruits might only grow deep in the brambles as well. In my game I made Hera Pears only grow off the path to add a little danger to their harvest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I can see this also. As I read in corebook that Hedge regions with low Lost population are mostly outgrown with Thorns, I will use it in mine game. Town is small ( only 2500, or so, citizens ) and PCs are first Lost to return to it. Hedge in here will be wild and untamed. And trods left are only those used by the Gentry on regular basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/405295-navigation-in-hedge?p=406189#post406189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, whatever you've moved Clarities bonus/penalties to perception and kenning onto should be what you base the Clarity rules in the hedge on. If it's tagged onto your new Integrity mechanic then just use that, even if it does change regularly. If you've gotten rid of those mechanics entirely... Well I'm not sure what you'd want to do about that at this moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Dichotomy</b> is not about perception, at least in direct way. It was one of the things I hated in original Clarity - morality stat based on idea of understanding what is real. Dichotomy is based on struggle between your memories of mortal life and fae instincs/desieres - it's based on idea of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/one-foot-in-flesh-and-one-in-spirit/\" target=\"_blank\">new Harmony</a> for <b>Werewolf</b> 2ed. There are not any &quot;when you hit low, you end game&quot; Well, it's not true - they are <b>two</b> extremes. On Dichotomy 10 you forget you are fae and try to repress your otherworldly side that much, so you can kill for it. ( Think about Peter from the beginning of <i>Hook</i> movie ) On Dichotomy 0 you work practically as little True Fae, at least psychologically. Most character are somewhere in between, rising and lowering in part of play - becoming more or less human/fae. If any Perception bonuses would be, they be in the middle of the scale - at ratings 3-7, with 5 having the most ones. But I'm not sure on those.<br /> <br /> I proposed the <i>Wits+Wyrd</i> roll for going by the Thorns, as this Dicepool is used to sense a magic of Glamour in Tokens. I could made case also for roll akin to <i>Inteligence+Composure</i> ( the &quot;Memory roll&quot; of nWoD ), maybe <i>Composure+Wyrd</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-15-2015, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:12:21-08:00","id":410058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/405295-navigation-in-hedge?p=406334#post406334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, it's clearing things up to me. If I change a Freehold area, I use the Intelligence + Survival. When I found correct &quot;region&quot; - I use the Intelligence + Investigation + Wyrd to find a gateway. In mine example - as character do not leave the region ( their hometown Hedge ) and only looks for the nearest way out, just use &quot;Gataway roll&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> Do keep in mind tho that the hedge still has it's complexity. A gateway to the hedge remains &quot;linked&quot; even if one of both sides of the gate move so I could create a door into the hedge in NY and then carry the hedge side of that door to the Hollow of a London based motley while shipping the earth side door to LA. Now we have a door from LA to a Hollow reflecting London. In that case if you go through the gate from LA to Hollow and then do a Gateway roll you'd wind up with a gate out into London.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/405295-navigation-in-hedge?p=406334#post406334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about situation when they are actively hunting for the Goblin Fruits ( the are almost dead, they need their healing )? I assume looking for those is with the Intelligence+Survival? But if finding the clues for specific Gates is based on Investigation, maybe looking for the clues of Goblin Fruits should also?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I run looking for goblin fruits as a survival skill, similar to finding mundane food in a mundane forest. Hence Survival. Gata know your plants and animals to know <i>which</i> you can eat. On a related note I'd assume everything in the hedge is a goblin fruit is so far as it's magic and eating it is libel to do weird things. It's just that most of the things you might stick in your mouth will do something bad so you're looking for the ones that are good.<br /> <br /> My take on using Investigation for finding gateways is that you're looking for subtle clues as to the transition in worlds, basically things that don't quite belong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/405295-navigation-in-hedge?p=406334#post406334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I proposed the <i>Wits+Wyrd</i> roll for going by the Thorns, as this Dicepool is used to sense a magic of Glamour in Tokens. I could made case also for roll akin to <i>Inteligence+Composure</i> ( the &quot;Memory roll&quot; of nWoD ), maybe <i>Composure+Wyrd</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Composure + Wyrd makes the most sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T23:52:21-08:00","id":413863,"title":"","content":"For others looking on rules of Navigation or Time in Hedge, <b>Kings Raven</b>'s <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Dream Catchers</i></a> Hunter fan supplement has detailed and extended rules on those on 148 till 155. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> He propose then roll of Resolve+Wyrd for Visualizing of Destination for journey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T00:29:57-08:00","id":413875,"title":"","content":"It's not &quot;my&quot; supplement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> it was a group effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}